256:        <p>A <em>Slater point</em> of (P) is a point \(\bar x\) that satisfies each inequality strictly, \(g_i(\bar x) < 0\), and each equality exactly, \(h_j(\bar x) = 0\). Slater's condition is the statement that a Slater point exists. It is the hypothesis of Open item 3.2 in Lesson 3, the necessity statement, which this lesson does not use.</p>
